stateDiagram-v2
  [*] --> Idle
  Idle --> Armed : pointer or keyboard intent
  Armed --> Running : primary user gesture
  Running --> Stopped : stop or route change
  Stopped --> Armed : new gesture
  Stopped --> [*]

  state Running {
    [*] --> Drone
    Drone --> Practice : start the theka
    Practice --> Drone : stop the theka
    --
    [*] --> Audible
    Audible --> Muted : mute
    Muted --> Audible : unmute
    --
    state MotionChoice <<choice>>
    [*] --> MotionChoice
    MotionChoice --> Animated : motion allowed
    MotionChoice --> Static : prefers-reduced-motion
    Animated --> Static : preference changes
    Static --> Animated : preference changes
  }

  note right of Idle : No AudioContext exists until a user gesture
  note right of Armed : AudioContext is created and resumed inside the gesture handler
  note right of Running : Mute and reduced motion are parallel flags, not lifecycle exits
  note right of Stopped : Context is suspended, not destroyed, so a gesture can resume it
